1
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,700
Ah! Miss Stewart! Welcome!

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:10,900
How are you?

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:11,800
Fine, Somsak. And you?

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,100
Fine, thank you.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,200
This is my friend Harry Bennett.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,000
Pleased to meet you.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,800
Very nice to meet you.

8
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,123
Any friend of Miss Stewart's is welcome at Somsak's.

9
00:00:20,123 --> 00:00:22,500
Follow me, please.

10
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:23,412
I like it here.

11
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:27,400
I do, too. I come here often.

12
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,998
A special place for special people.

13
00:00:29,998 --> 00:00:33,700
Thank you, Somsak.

14
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:39,800
Well! Nice restaurant.

15
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,200
Would you like something to drink?

16
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,000
Yes, I'd like a glass of ginger ale with ice.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:45,964
Harry, what would you like?

18
00:00:45,964 --> 00:00:47,500
Do you have a dry white wine?

19
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,262
How about a California chablis?

20
00:00:49,262 --> 00:00:50,800
Chablis is fine.

21
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,000
What would you like to eat?

22
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,200
I'd like the mee krob.

23
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,600
Harry, would you like to see a menu?

24
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:57,900
No, it's Ok.

25
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:02,900
I'll have the mee krob also.

26
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:05,558
What is it?

27
00:01:05,558 --> 00:01:08,700
Crispy fried noodles. I love them.

28
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,100
May I bring you a salad?

29
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:11,300
Oh yes.

30
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:12,700
What do you recommend today?

31
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:14,800
I recommend rose-petal salad.

32
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,600
Special for new friends.

33
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:19,600
Rose-petal salad?

34
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,400
Why not?

35
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:26,300
I'll take care of everything.

36
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:28,683
I hope you're hungry.

37
00:01:28,683 --> 00:01:36,000
What? Oh, yes. Starving. Well, I...

38
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,600
Well, I ...

39
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,185
What do you do at Universe Toy Company?

40
00:01:42,185 --> 00:01:44,700
I'm the vice-president of new toy development.

41
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,880
Terrific!

42
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:49,100
I know you 're a CPA.

43
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,500
That's true. Harry Bennett,

44
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,800
certified public accountant.

45
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,200
I love numbers.

46
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,600
I do some work for Smith and Dale,

47
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:57,647
Your company's accounting firm.

48
00:01:57,647 --> 00:02:01,000
And so...

49
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,300
Here we are.

50
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:03,900
Yes.

51
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,300
I have a daughter.

52
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,700
I know. How old is she?

53
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:08,705
She's nine years old.

54
00:02:08,705 --> 00:02:10,700
That's a nice age. What's her name?

55
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,900
Michelle.

56
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:24,700
Do you have a picture of her?

57
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,600
She's very pretty.

58
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:33,800
Thank you.

59
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,300
Rose-petal salad.

60
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:39,600
And there's a phone call for you, Mr. Bennett.

61
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,200
Excuse me, Susan.

62
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:44,993
I hope nothing is wrong.

63
00:02:44,993 --> 00:02:46,300
I'll get the rest of the dinner.

64
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:59,800
Excuse me.

65
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,600
Please forgive me, Susan, but...

66
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:05,800
I have to leave. I feel terrible, but...

67
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:07,730
What's the matter?

68
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:09,500
My daughter isn't feeling well.

69
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,968
Oh no! Is it serious?

70
00:03:11,968 --> 00:03:15,900
I don't know. The baby-sitter says she has a stomachache,

71
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:16,600
and she's crying.

72
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,900
I'll have to go home.

73
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,098
Will you forgive me?

74
00:03:19,098 --> 00:03:21,900
Of course. I'm so sorry for Michelle.

75
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:23,900
And you didn't have a chance to eat.

76
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,200
Oh, it's OK.

77
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,100
Let me take you home first.

78
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:29,200
No, no. Please, go ahead.

79
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,600
It's our first date.

80
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,300
We'll make another.

81
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:35,100
Please don't worry.

82
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:35,700
I'll phone you.

83
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,600
I hope your daughter is all right. Good-bye.

84
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:42,600
Good-bye.
